e scalar sub-query into a LEFT JOIN operation with an aggregate function on the column(s) being selected in the sub-query. The original query structure is:\n\nSELECT ... FROM table1 WHERE column = (SELECT AGG_FUNCTION(column2) FROM table2 WHERE table1.join_column = table2.join_column)\n\nThe transformed query structure is:\n\nSELECT ... FROM table1 LEFT JOIN (SELECT join_column, AGG_FUNCTION(column2) AS agg_result FROM table2 GROUP BY join_column) AS sub_query ON table1.join_column = sub_query.join_column WHERE column = sub_query.agg_result\n\nIn the given SQL query, the scalar sub-query calculates the average return amount and then multiplies it by 1.2. The rewritten query uses a LEFT JOIN operation to calculate the average return amount for each store and then filters the results based on the condition > (average return amount * 1.2).', 'time': 19.783154010772705}
